scored: 0

card c05
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: Contaminated: material on or in
figure: contamination-figure
figure_at: 2

body:
    [[radioactive-contamination|Contamination]] is radioactive material on or in something, where it is not wanted. It can be on skin or clothes, breathed in or swallowed, or spread about a place.

card c06
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: The glitter is the problem

body:
    Radiation does not get on or in people. It is the material that spreads. That is how a person can be exposed to a source without being contaminated.

card c07
kind: item
type: item
item: u3-l3-tom-spread
connected: true

card c08
kind: item
type: item
item: u3-l3-choice-contaminated

card c09
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: When does it end?
figure: exposure-ends
figure_at: 1

body:
    Near a source, the exposure ends when you move away or the source is shielded. If radioactive material is on you, you are exposed until it is removed, and material on skin or clothes can often be washed off. If it is inside you, you are exposed until it leaves the body.

